      "doc": [
        "Verify a selected ML-DSA batch with one shared FIPS 204 context.",
        "",
        "`context` is a byte range within `messages`, of length at most 255. Message",
        "offsets still identify each row independently; the context is a zero-copy",
        "view and is framed as `0x00 || len(context) || context || message`. The",
        "context may overlap a message. Use separate batches for different contexts.",
        "All other inputs and results follow [`verify_batch_with_parameters`].",
        "",
        "Capture retains the message value and records the context range as semantic",
        "attributes. Rebinding that input also rebinds its context bytes. This is pure",
        "ML-DSA verification, not the distinct HashML-DSA prehash interface.",
        "",
        "# Errors",
        "",
        "Rejects reversed, out-of-bounds, or longer-than-255-byte context ranges,",
        "including for empty batches, plus the errors of [`verify_batch`]. This",
        "Experimental public-data route does not admit private-key execution."
      ],
